## Key observations from this flow

### Trace IDs propagate end to end
A single UUID attached at request start flows through every table: messages, events, tool_calls, cmem observations. Debugging is a matter of filtering by trace_id.

### claude-mem is consulted before Claude
Isaac queries claude-mem before sending to Claude API. This injects compressed historical context (yesterday's work, known conventions, relevant prior decisions) — saves context window, prevents relearning.

### Tool calls are sandwiched in the API loop
Claude's response is iterative: request → tool call → tool result → request → ... until done. Each tool call logs to `tool_calls` table with duration and success flag. This is where Sentinel sees agent behavior.

### Reflections happen on a separate cron
The 8 PM daily reflection is its own cycle — doesn't interrupt interactive work. Isaac generates his reflection by querying his day's logs, asking Claude to synthesize, committing to the genesis-config repo.

### Nothing touches disk unsafely
Every write is either: SQLite (atomic, transactional), git (commit + push), or Claude API (authenticated). No unencrypted state leaves the P14s.
